                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "spherical":</h3><p><b>Spherical</b> microphones are built in the shape of a sphere. </p><p>Mounting a transducer on the surface of a sphere affects the frequency response of the transducer, due to the way sound waves flow around a spherical surface. </p><p>See also <a href="http://recordinghacks.com/microphones/tag/spherical-capsule">spherical-capsule microphones</a>, which can be built into bodies of any shape, but which mount their transducers onto a small sphere (the diameter of which is usually about 4cm) &#8212; again, to take advantage of the affects of the sphere on the transducer&#8217;s response.</p>
